    [618] = {
        achievementId = 618,
        name = "Putting Out the Light",
        category = "PvP",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Putting Out the Light",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Defeat an enemy-capital leader, handling guards, defending players and any needed group coordination.\n\n1. Use a HORDE character and travel to the ORIGINAL Azuremyst Isle and Exodar. Bring a group with healing and enough damage if your character cannot sustain a long fight. Prophet Velen's non-hostile quest appearances elsewhere are not this city-leader objective.\n\n2. Enter the Exodar and follow its passages to the Vault of Lights. If arriving from the island's harbor, use the nearby city entrance into this quarter. Avoid accidentally pulling extra groups while assembling the party.\n\n3. Find Prophet Velen around 32.5, 54.5 on the EXODAR city map. Clear his guards and place your back against a nearby wall to limit knockback. Keep the fight inside his room so he does not leash and reset.\n\n4. Damage Velen, deal with respawning defenders and interrupt his interruptible heals. If a yellow healing pool appears under him, MOVE HIM OUT OF IT without dragging him far enough to reset. A recent Retail comment reports Vigilant Defenders returning during long fights and protecting him with an immunity buff: kill those defenders when they appear.\n\n5. Defeat Velen and check the achievement while close enough for credit. If his health keeps recovering, solve the healing-pool or defender problem rather than repeating damage into the protection. Older comments' Auberdine boat route and fixed raid-size or gear requirements are obsolete.",
        stepCount = 5,
        waypoints = {
