        },
        itemId = 30480,
        name = "Fiery Warhorse's Reins",
        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A rare boss drop and daily or weekly loot lockouts make the number of attempts unpredictable.\n\n1. Travel to Karazhan in Deadwind Pass and enter the ORIGINAL raid through the ground-level gatehouse at 46.9, 74.8. Do not enter the raised Legion Return to Karazhan dungeon portal: that instance has a different Attumen and a different mount.\n\n2. Stay on the entry floor and follow the stables corridor toward Midnight and Attumen, around 45.2, 82.6 on the original Servant's Quarters map. Clear the spectral horses and stable hands along the way so their fears and stuns do not drag extra packs into the encounter. You do not need to complete the rest of the tower.\n\n3. Attack Midnight to begin the encounter, defeat Attumen when he joins, and loot Attumen's corpse for a chance at Fiery Warhorse's Reins. Check the body even if you defeated the encounter almost instantly on a high-level character.\n\n4. If the reins do not drop, return after the weekly raid reset or make another attempt on a different eligible character. Reset All Instances does not refresh this character's boss loot. No old Karazhan attunement or Master's Key quest is required for this run.\n\n5. Use Fiery Warhorse's Reins from your bags to learn Fiery Warhorse. This is a ground mount; it does not fly like the Headless Horseman's mount or share the collection entry of Midnight's Eternal Reins.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=882",
        difficultyReason = "A rare boss drop and daily or weekly loot lockouts make the number of attempts unpredictable.",
        difficulty = "hard",
        achievementId = 882,
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=882#comments",
    },
    [883] = {
        source = "Anzu - Heroic Sethekk Halls, Halls of Mourning",
        category = "Dungeon and Raids",
        faction = "all",
        npcId = 23035,
        requirements = "Heroic Sethekk Halls access; a character capable of clearing the route and Anzu. No Druid summon requirement.",
        cost = "No purchase cost for the dungeon-drop route.",
        tips = "Normal Sethekk Halls is not the direct mount-farming difficulty. The old Druid summoning instructions predate Retail's permanently present Anzu. Daily attempts on multiple characters increase the number of chances, without guaranteeing a drop. Obtain and learn the mount on this account. The feat may trigger when the reins are looted; its Feat of Strength category does not mean this mount has been removed.",
        waypoints = {
            {
                mapID = 108,
                x = 0.449,
                y = 0.6559999999999999,
                step = 1,
                label = "Sethekk Halls - eastern Auchindoun entrance; Heroic",
            },
            {
                mapID = 259,
                x = 0.326,
                y = 0.545,
                step = 3,
                label = "Anzu - permanently present Heroic mount boss",
                mapName = "Sethekk Halls: Halls of Mourning",
            },
        },
        itemId = 32768,
        name = "Reins of the Raven Lord",
        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A rare boss drop and daily or weekly loot lockouts make the number of attempts unpredictable.\n\n1. Before entering, right-click your character portrait and set Dungeon Difficulty to HEROIC. Travel to the Auchindoun ring in Terokkar Forest and enter Sethekk Halls on its eastern side at 44.9, 65.6. The other Auchindoun entrances lead to different dungeons.\n\n2. Follow the Veil Sethekk corridors past Darkweaver Syth's area and climb to the Halls of Mourning floor. Clear enemies that follow you, especially the Sethekk packs whose control effects can interrupt a run. A Rogue or Druid can stealth past avoidable trash, but no particular class is required.\n\n3. Find Anzu in his room at 32.6, 54.5 on Halls of Mourning. He is already present in Retail: no Druid, old summon item or flight-form quest is needed. Defeat him and loot Reins of the Raven Lord. If he becomes immune during a longer fight, kill his summoned birds, then finish the boss.\n\n4. If the reins do not drop, leave and return after the next daily Heroic reset, or use another eligible character. Killing Talon King Ikiss is optional for the mount chance. Reset All Instances does not grant a second Anzu kill's loot on the same daily save.\n\n5. Use the reins from your bags to learn Raven Lord and check Collections > Mounts. Despite the bird appearance, this is a ground mount and cannot fly.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=883",
        difficultyReason = "A rare boss drop and daily or weekly loot lockouts make the number of attempts unpredictable.",
        difficulty = "hard",
        achievementId = 883,
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        sourceURL = "https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=883#comments",
    },
    [884] = {
        source = "Kael'thas Sunstrider - original Heroic Magisters' Terrace",
        category = "Dungeon and Raids",
        faction = "all",
        npcId = 24664,
        requirements = "Access to the original Isle of Quel'Danas and Heroic Magisters' Terrace; no racial reputation requirement.",
        cost = "No purchase cost for the dungeon-drop route.",
        tips = "Both factions can learn and use this drop. It is separate from the Horde-only Swift Warstrider sold for PvP tokens. The Shattrath portal and original island are still usable Retail destinations; the pins intentionally use the original island and dungeon floors. Obtain and learn the mount on this account. The feat may trigger when the reins are looted; its Feat of Strength category does not mean this mount has been removed.",
