    [896] = {
        achievementId = 896,
        name = "A Quest a Day Keeps the Ogres at Bay",
        category = "Reputation",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "A Quest a Day Keeps the Ogres at Bay",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Unlock both Ogri'la daily hubs and repeat their limited quests across many daily resets.\n\n1. Fly to Ogri'la on the western Blade's Edge plateau (28.8, 57.4), enable Trivial Quests and speak to Chu'a'lor. Complete The Crystals by gathering 5 Apexis Shards from nearby creatures. Follow An Apexis Relic: spend a shard at a relic and reproduce its flashing color sequence, adding each new flash to the previous sequence.\n\n2. Complete Our Boy Wants To Be A Skyguard Ranger for Torkus: gather the required Apexis Shards and use a Fel Crystalforge at Forge Camp: Wrath to obtain the Unstable Flask of the Beast. Follow The Skyguard Outpost to the camp just north of Ogri'la (27.5, 52.6). Complete the introductory Bombing Run and Wrangle Some Aether Rays! quests to unlock their repeatable versions.\n\n3. Each day, take Bomb Them Again! from Vanderlip. Bomb 15 cannonball stacks at Forge Camp: Wrath, north of the outpost, using the supplied Skyguard Bombs while mounted. Aim at the ammunition piles, not the demons or cannons. Return to the outpost to turn in.\n\n4. Complete Wrangle More Aether Rays! by using the supplied rope on five different wild rays near the outpost. Retail allows wrangling them at full health; do not kill the rays first. At Ogri'la, also complete The Relic's Emanation by repeating the full sequence at an Apexis Relic. Write down each new color if needed.\n\n5. At Honored, complete Banish the Demons to unlock Banish More Demons. Place the supplied portal at a forge camp, bring living demons close to it, wait for its debuff and then kill them. Killing demons outside the portal's influence does not count.\n\n6. Repeat the three available dailies, then all four after Honored, until Ogri'la is Exalted. Shartuul's Darkrune event is removed and is not a Retail shortcut. Ordinary kills do not provide an unlimited reputation grind; applicable reputation bonuses can shorten the daily schedule.",
