    [1192] = {
        achievementId = 1192,
        name = "Nagrand Slam",
        category = "Quests",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Nagrand Slam",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Finish the named zone's story chapters and their quest prerequisites; legacy combat alone does not complete them.\n\n1. Use Nagrand in OUTLAND and enable Trivial Quests. Track the eight story chapters for your faction. Start at Telaar; the achievement follows completed stories, not the old 75/85-quest total. Do not substitute Halaa repeatables or unrelated Shadowmoon quests for a missing chapter.\n\n2. For The Adventures of Corki, take HELP! from Corki's Burning Blade Ruins cage (72.5, 70.7), obtain the Boulderfist Key from the local ogres and free him. Report to Arechron in Telaar for Corki's Gone Missing Again!, then rescue him at the back of Northwind Cleft (39.3, 27.4). Return for Corki's Ransom, find his Warmaul Hill cage and take Cho'war the Pillager. The key comes from Cho'war in the upper cave system; return to Corki's cage after looting it. One rescue does not complete all three adventures.\n\n3. For Lantresor of the Blade, follow your faction's Diplomatic Measures to Lantresor in Burning Blade Ruins (73.8, 62.6). Complete Ruthless Cunning and Armaments for Deception, then Returning the Favor / Body of Evidence and the final message back to your faction town. Use the supplied banners/bodies for the quest objectives instead of just clearing the camp.\n\n4. For Throne of the Elements, finish the elementalists' Skysong, earth and fire chains. Continue Gordawg's The Tortured Earth -> Eating Damnation -> Shattering the Veil -> Gurok the Usurper; collect the ogre skulls and summon Gurok at Warmaul Hill. Also loot The Howling Wind from air elementals, start its quest and finish Bring Me the Egg! and its follow-up where offered. Drop-started quests can be the missing link.\n\n5. For The Murkblood, complete the Sunspring / captive rescue quests from your faction town. Kill the mounted Murkblood Invaders traveling in groups of three, LOOT their invasion plans and start the resulting quest. Finish Telaar's Murkblood reports and the captive escort; the mounted invaders' item chain is separate from simply killing the village mobs.\n\n6. For Threats to Nagrand, complete all WANTED poster quests in your town, ending with Durn the Hungerer. ALSO finish Altruis the Sufferer's forge-camp chain from 27.3, 43: Survey the Land, Buying Time, The Master Planner, Patience and Understanding and Forge Camp: Annihilated. Patience and Understanding sends you to Sal'salabim in Shattrath's Lower City tavern; that trip is required even if no obvious map marker appears.\n\n7. For Encountering the Ethereals, visit Aeris Landing (30.8, 58.2), finish Zerid's Matters of Security and Gava'xi, and turn in the crystal/ivory introductions offered by the nearby Consortium NPCs. Follow the single-use story quests; repeating membership/reputation hand-ins is not a replacement.\n\n8. For The Ring of Blood, speak to Gurgthock (42.7, 20.7). Complete all six arena quests in order, through The Final Challenge. Stay inside the arena for each spawned opponent and return to the quest giver between fights; killing an unrelated ogre outside the event gives no arena progress.\n\n9. For The Ultimate Bloodsport, take all three Mastery chains at Nesingwary Safari (71.5, 40.7). Each chain has two hunting stages and its named hunt: Banthar, Bach'lor or Gutripper. After turning in all three, take The Ultimate Bloodsport, kill Tusker (44.4, 65.9), loot the heart and return to Hemet. The separate Hills Like White Elekk guide details these hunts.\n\n10. Check all eight chapters after their final hand-ins. If Threats is missing, check BOTH the WANTED poster and Altruis; if Murkblood is missing, look for the mounted invaders' dropped plans. If Corki is missing, return to Arechron for the next rescue instead of repeating the first cage.",
        stepCount = 10,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 107, x = 0.545, y = 0.723, step = 1, label = "Telaar - faction introductions" },
