    [1195] = {
        achievementId = 1195,
        name = "Shadow of the Betrayer",
        category = "Quests",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Shadow of the Betrayer",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Complete Shadowmoon's long branching story, dungeon errands and scripted quest chains.\n\n1. Use Shadowmoon Valley in OUTLAND, not Draenor. Enable Trivial Quests and track your faction's eight chapters. Choose Aldor OR Scryers through Khadgar's City of Light chain in Shattrath if you have not already; the choice opens required Shadowmoon quests. Keep the provided disguises, spectacles, totems and quest weapons until their chains finish.\n\n2. For Wildhammer Stronghold (Alliance) or Shadowmoon Village (Horde), follow your base's Legion Hold investigation through its infernal-bombing tasks, then the Deathforge chain. Defeat Warbringer Razuun inside the Deathforge, continue Gaining Access with the weaponsmith's key and the Invasion Point: Cataclysm fel-reaver objective, then turn in News of Victory. Enter the Deathforge through its cave and interior gate rather than searching above its underground quest marker.\n\n3. For The First Death Knight, follow Zorus the Judicator (Alliance) or Chief Apothecary Hildagard (Horde) into the ghost investigation. Wear the supplied Spectrecles when looking for spectres. Continue Teron Gorefiend - Lore and Legend, collect the requested cloak, truncheon and armor in its three divination branches, then finish Teron Gorefiend, I am.... Removing the spectacles can hide the very enemies/items you need.\n\n4. For The Dark Conclave, finish your base's Sketh'lon Wreckage investigation and find Parshah, the Sketh'lon deserter on the central road. Follow his Asghar / Rod of Lianthe / feathers tasks through Imbuing the Headpiece and Thwart the Dark Conclave. Use the completed quest headpiece at the ritual site; ordinary kills around the wreckage are only the opening of the story.\n\n5. For The Cipher of Damnation, start Earthmender Torlok at the Altar of Damnation (42.2, 45). Complete the fire/earth, water and air spirit quests: plant the supplied totem near the enemies BEFORE killing them so it can capture their souls. Follow Oronok Torn-heart at his northern farm; use his whistle near living boars to dig up tubers, then finish A Lesson Learned and The Cipher of Damnation - Truth and History.\n\n6. Complete ALL THREE sons' branches. Grom'tor in Coilskar needs naga keys to open footlockers for his fragment. Ar'tor at Illidari Point needs the Demonic Crystal Prisons / Lohn'goron bow chain before his fragment. Borak near Eclipse Point sends you through Of Thistleheads and Eggs... to Tobias in Shattrath; return with the bloodthistle, lure the target, then finish Shadowmoon Shuffle, the Ruusk disguise conversation and Ruul the Darkener for the third fragment. Do not attack a target you are meant to speak to while disguised.\n\n7. Return all three fragments to Oronok, then bring the assembled Cipher to the Altar of Damnation. Speak to Oronok there to begin the event, remain for the dialogue and defeat Cyrukh when the fight becomes active. Finish the final hand-in; possessing the fragments without completing this event leaves the chapter unfinished.\n\n8. For Anti-Demon Weapons, kill Overseer Ripsaw near Legion Hold and loot the Illidari-Bane Shard to START its quest. Report to your faction base, finish Capture the Weapons, then visit David Wayne at Wayne's Refuge in TEROKKAR (77.6, 38.6). Bring him 1 Adamantite Frame, 4 Heavy Knothide Leather and 1 Demon Warding Totem; Fantei in Shattrath's Lower City sells the totem.\n\n9. Accept Wayne's dungeon material quests BEFORE entering. In The Mechanar, take the right hallway and look by the wall near Mechano-Lord Capacitus for the lootable Overcharged Manacell boxes; the item is not a final-boss drop. In Shadow Labyrinth, loot Grandmaster Vorpil for The Lexicon Demonica. Turn BOTH quests in to unlock the next pair: Hydromancer Thespia in Steamvault supplies Underworld Loam, and Warbringer O'mrogg in Shattered Halls supplies Tear of the Earthmother. Return both to Wayne.\n\n10. Finish The Bane of the Illidari, then Quenching the Blade. Take the supplied blade to the Scalding Pools high on the Hand of Gul'dan and use it in the lava; stay for the resulting defense/event. Return the quenched blade to David Wayne. Merely clearing the four dungeons does not finish Anti-Demon Weapons without these final steps.\n\n11. For Borrowed Power, take Karabor Training Grounds from your chosen faction's Shadowmoon camp: Altar of Sha'tar for Aldor, Sanctum of the Stars for Scryers. Finish A Necessary Distraction and follow Altruis to Nagrand (27.3, 43). Complete Against the Legion (Netherstorm), Against the Illidari (Shadowmoon) and Against All Odds (Zangarmarsh) using their quest items and marked targets.\n\n12. Return to Altruis, listen to Illidan's Pupil and accept The Book of Fel Names. Enter Shadow Labyrinth and loot BLACKHEART THE INCITER for the book, then return to Altruis. This is a different boss/item from Wayne's Lexicon, which comes from VORPIL. Finish the report to your Aldor/Scryer camp and Varedis Must Be Stopped at Black Temple's training grounds.\n\n13. For Akama's Promise, follow Tablets of Baa'ri -> Oronu the Elder -> The Ashtongue Corruptors, including all four corruptors, then The Warden's Cage. Enter through the FLOOR GRATE at 57.4, 49.7. Finish Sanoru's Proof of Allegiance against Zandras, return, swim down the passage and take the right-hand route to Akama's chamber.\n\n14. Akama sends you to Seer Udalo in The Arcatraz: find Udalo's BODY inside, before the final boss area, and accept A Mysterious Portent. Return to Akama, complete the Atamal Terrace Soulstealer/Shadowlord Deathwail event for the Heart of Fury, return to Akama and take Akama's Promise to A'dal in Shattrath. The zone chapter does not require the later Black Temple raid attunement chain.\n\n15. For Netherwing Ledge, start Mordenai's Kindness in Netherwing Fields, follow the flying Neltharaku's crystals/drake-rescue quests and free Karynaku from Zuluhed at Dragonmaw Fortress. Complete Ally of the Netherwing, Blood Oath of the Netherwing and In Service of the Illidari into the disguised base camp. On the island's eastern side, kill Arvoar the Rapacious around 74.6, 86.7 and loot the Partially Digested Hand. Start A Job Unfinished..., kill its 10 Overmine Flayers and Barash the Den Mother, then return to Mor'ghor. This chapter needs that story, not Netherwing Exalted, daily repetition or an egg grind.\n\n16. Check the eight chapter criteria and complete outstanding final reports. Normal difficulty is sufficient for these original dungeon quests; old Heroic keys and raid attunements are unnecessary. If combining trips, have BOTH Shadow Labyrinth item quests active so Blackheart's book and Vorpil's Lexicon can be collected in the same run.",
