        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Collect a complete class appearance set through random weekly raid drops and the relevant token exchanges.\n\n1. Open Collections > Appearances > Sets and select a complete Tier 5 appearance set for an original Burning Crusade class. Pin down its missing slots before farming; five tier pieces alone may leave required matching boots, belt or bracers unfinished.\n\n2. In Serpentshrine Cavern, kill Lady Vashj for the helm, Leotheras the Blind for gloves and Fathom-Lord Karathress for legs. The entrance is through Coilfang Reservoir's underwater pipe in Zangarmarsh.\n\n3. In The Eye, the central Tempest Keep raid in Netherstorm, kill Void Reaver for shoulders and Kael'thas for the chest. Loot trash as well: some matching set slots come from non-tier drops or crafted items.\n\n4. Use eligible class tokens to create the armor, choosing the appropriate loot specialization. Where a token offers a choice, collect the PvE appearance, not its alternative PvP reward. A modern class with no original tier set cannot create that old class's tier pieces for itself.\n\n5. For every remaining slot in the SETS tab, inspect its specific appearance source and farm or craft that item. Matching off-pieces vary by class. Repeat after weekly resets for random drops; the armor set's visual checklist, not just its set-bonus count, is the goal.\n\n6. Permanently learn the final appearances. A trade/refund timer can delay credit. If all slots are learned but the achievement has not refreshed, relog; comments also report applying the complete set as a transmog refreshes credit. Do not buy or delete duplicate items before checking the actual missing slot.",
